      "description": "The Global Wind Atlas provides wind climate statistics on a 250 m grid worldwide. It is produced in two stages: a WRF mesoscale simulation driven by reanalysis boundary conditions, followed by microscale downscaling that accounts for terrain and roughness. The two-stage derivation is why it appears independent of a reanalysis-derived time series and is not — the reanalysis is two hops upstream rather than one, which is exactly the depth an unbounded provenance walk is needed to find.",
